If I read the other post correctly, the dump log entries are
not randomized.  Rather, when the bones file is loaded, the
items in the bones pile are alphabetized based on their
identity in the new game.  So, for example, a wand known in
the new game as an iron wand would be ordered prior to one
that is now a zinc wand.  Thus, the order in the pile might
not match the dump log, even though the order in the dump
log itself is unchanged, because the dump log was generated
based on the old game, with no knowledge of what the random
names of those items would eventually become in some later
game when they were loaded as a bones pile.


